  "notes": "{彫|ほ}る means to carve or engrave into a hard surface.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: {像|ぞう}を{彫|ほ}る\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {彫刻|ちょうこく}: sculpture, carving\n- {木彫|きぼ}り: woodcarving\n- {彫|ほ}り{物|もの}: carving, engraving\n- {彫|ほ}りが{深|ふか}い: having well-defined features (of a face)\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n- {掘|ほ}る (to dig) has the same reading but different meaning and kanji.\n- {彫|ほ}る: to carve INTO a surface\n- {掘|ほ}る: to dig OUT from the ground",
